      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Built in 1899, the Morristown Hotel is listed on the National Register of Historic Places and remains a town icon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://aare.com/morristown-az/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Morristown served as a staging area for supplies and workers during the early 1900s construction of the Arizona and California Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://yancearizona.com/morristown-arizona-a-hidden-gem-in-the-desert/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Just north of town, Castle Hot Springs offers a glimpse into Arizona’s early resort history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://aare.com/morristown-az/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s historic downtown showcases architecture and landmarks that echo Morristown’s rich past.",
